<p>Garlic is the best stinky herb in the world and a true gift from God. It is nature’s antibiotic.</p>
<p>Try gently roasting an entire bulb of garlic in a medium oven for as long as it takes the cloves to become soft and creamy in texture. Allow them to cool a little, then squeeze the goodness from each papery shell and spread on bread or vegetables. Sprinkle with herb salt. Also goes well incorporated into salad dressings.</p>
<p>Delicious!</p>
<p>No one who partakes of this delicacy with you will be aware of any odour. Everyone else can have some too, or go sit elsewhere.</p>
